{"title":"1976 Canadian MO Problems/Problem 1","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1976_Canadian_MO_Problems/Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Given four weights in geometric progression and an equal arm balance, show how to find the heaviest weight using the balance only twice.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1976_Canadian_MO_Problems/Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Note that for any 4 weights <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/0/0/20017e918ce1fe395cb4f1b778ee88f409ff27e1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a,ar,ar^2,ar^3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"105\" height=\"20\" />, the heaviest weight, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/c/d/4cdab5f83e6ea0db9893d1cafe454a860a7e8680.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ar^3$\" width=\"24\" height=\"15\" />, always dominates on the balance when these 4 weights are measured with two weights on both sides. I like to tackle these problems by putting some numbers in.Let the 4 weights be 1kg, 2kg, 4kg, and 8kg. \n</p><p>Step 1:\nWhen split into 2 groups, whichever side is heavier must contain the 8kg weight. \n</p><p>Step 2:\nNow put the two object that weighed more combined on two sides of the balance, and the one heavier is the heaviest object among the four.\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=User:Promising_wind&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"User:Promising wind (page does not exist)\">Promising wind</a> (<a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=User_talk:Promising_wind&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"User talk:Promising wind (page does not exist)\">talk</a>) 18:16, 3 April 2026 (EDT)\n</p>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"clear:both; margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1976_Canadian_MO\" title=\"1976 Canadian MO\">1976 Canadian MO</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1976_Canadian_MO_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"1976 Canadian MO Problems (page does not exist)\">Problems</a></b>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"33%\" align=\"center\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b>First Problem</b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"34%\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1976_Canadian_MO_Problems/Problem_2&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"1976 Canadian MO Problems/Problem 2 (page does not exist)\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1976_Canadian_MO_Problems/Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"1976 Canadian MO Problems/Problem 3 (page does not exist)\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1976_Canadian_MO_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"1976 Canadian MO Problems/Problem 4 (page does not exist)\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1976_Canadian_MO_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"1976 Canadian MO Problems/Problem 5 (page does not exist)\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1976_Canadian_MO_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"1976 Canadian MO Problems/Problem 6 (page does not exist)\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1976_Canadian_MO_Problems/Problem_7&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"1976 Canadian MO Problems/Problem 7 (page does not exist)\">7</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1976_Canadian_MO_Problems/Problem_8&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"1976 Canadian MO Problems/Problem 8 (page does not exist)\">8</a>\n</td>\n<td width=\"33%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1976_Canadian_MO_Problems/Problem_2&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"1976 Canadian MO Problems/Problem 2 (page does not exist)\">Problem 2</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<p><br />\n</p>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017172229\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: []\nCPU time usage: 0.014 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.022 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 37/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 879/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 59/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 331/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    6.599      1 Template:Old_CanadaMO_box_(6-8_Problems)/8\n100.00%    6.599      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:35855:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261017172229 and revision id 280685. Rendering was triggered because: api-parse\n -->\n</div>"}